Voice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":" key whose value a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination reads from the record’s context: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ApplicationKey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DeviceKey"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/OperatingSystemKey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/LocaleKey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/NetworkKey"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext\/VendorIdentifierKey"},{"type":"text","text":". The first five are in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Events"},{"type":"text","text":" module, as a store keeps them beside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each record, so a record recovered after a relaunch carries the values it was tracked with. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module reads the values the platform reports."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The app, device, operating system and locale are read once, when the enricher is made, never per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event. The network connection changes while the app runs, so on Apple platforms ","type":"text"},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" starts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NWPathMonitor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its own and sets the latest connection on each record. Give each tracker its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own call. Off Apple platforms there is no device and no path monitor, so those two enrichers set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, and a server or tool, whose process usually has no Info.plist, passes its own app to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"application(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":", made on the main actor, adds the platform’s identifier for vendor as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value. It is the one identifier here that outlives a session, so add it only when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app has decided to and has the user’s consent. It is never stored or made up: on macOS and Linux,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which have none, records carry no key, and a store never writes it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For the session an event was tracked in, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sessions"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import StandardContext","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.application(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","\/\/ A destination reads each value from the record's context:","\/\/ record.context[ApplicationKey.self]?.version, record.context[OperatingSystemKey.self]?.name"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers each value and the identifier for vendor in more detail."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/standardco